---
// Step 8: controls bound to the agent's code in the playground (see learn/playground.ts, `data-control`).
---

<div class="learn-controls">
  <label class="wide">
    <span>System text</span>
    <textarea data-control="system" rows="2"></textarea>
  </label>
  <label>
    <span>Budget tokens</span>
    <input type="number" min="1" step="10" data-control="budgetTokens" />
    <small>What one request may cost, the system text included.</small>
  </label>
  <label>
    <span>Memory</span>
    <select data-control="memory">
      <option value="window">windowMemory</option>
      <option value="last">lastMessages (yours)</option>
    </select>
    <small>Which layer provides Memory: the window drops whole turns, oldest first; lastMessages, in tiny-memory.ts, keeps the last n messages (n: 1 when picked here). The conversation goes on either way.</small>
  </label>
</div>
<p class="learn-note" data-controls-note hidden>
  A control is greyed out when its line is missing from your code. Press Reset in the Code pane to bring it back.
</p>
